                <h2>10. California and other US states</h2>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Categories collected in the past 12 months:</strong> identifiers (advertising ID, app-instance ID, IP address); internet or other electronic network activity (ad interactions, app usage events); approximate geolocation (derived from IP address); device information. Sources: your device, through the Google SDKs. Purposes: Section 4.</li>
                    <li><strong>Sale or sharing:</strong> we do not sell personal information for money. Making identifiers and ad interaction data available to Google for targeted advertising may count as "selling" or "sharing" under California and other state laws. <strong>Do Not Sell or Share My Personal Information:</strong> open Settings &gt; Privacy choices in the App and choose the opt-out in Google's US-state privacy message. You can also limit tracking with the device settings in Section 7.</li>
                    <li><strong>Sensitive personal information:</strong> we do not collect or use it.</li>
                    <li><strong>Your rights:</strong> to know, access, correct and delete personal information, to opt out of sale or sharing, and not to be discriminated against for using these rights. Send requests to <a href="#" data-email-user="support" data-email-domain="pifl-labs.com"><span class="email-text">support (at) pifl-labs.com</span></a>. Because your spending data never leaves your device, you can view, export or delete it directly in the App.</li>
                    <li>We do not knowingly sell or share personal information of consumers under 16.</li>
                </ul>

                <h2>11. Retention</h2>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Data on your device:</strong> kept until you delete it in the App or uninstall the App.</li>
                    <li><strong>Backup files you create:</strong> kept wherever you saved them until you delete them; uninstalling the App does not delete them.</li>
                    <li><strong>Data received by Google (AdMob, Firebase):</strong> retained by Google according to its policies (<a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/retention" target="_blank" rel="noopener">https://policies.google.com/technologies/retention</a>). We use analytics data only in aggregated form.</li>
                    <li><strong>Emails to support:</strong> kept for 3 years after your request is resolved, then deleted, unless the law requires us to keep them longer.</li>
                </ul>

                <h2>12. International transfer</h2>
                <p>Information collected by Google AdMob and Google Analytics for Firebase is sent over the internet from your device to Google LLC (United States) when you use the App, and is processed in the United States and other countries where Google operates. For transfers from the EEA, UK and Switzerland, Google relies on safeguards recognized by data protection law, such as the EU–U.S. Data Privacy Framework and standard contractual clauses. You can avoid personalized-ad processing as described in Section 7, or stop all transfers by uninstalling the App.</p>

                <h2>13. Children</h2>
                <p>The App is not directed to children under 13 (under 16 in the EEA). We do not knowingly collect personal information from children. If you believe a child has used the App and you want related information deleted, contact us at <a href="#" data-email-user="support" data-email-domain="pifl-labs.com"><span class="email-text">support (at) pifl-labs.com</span></a>.</p>

                <h2>14. Your rights</h2>
                <p>Depending on where you live, you may have the right to access, correct, delete, restrict or object to the processing of your personal information, to data portability, to withdraw consent at any time, and to complain to a data protection authority. Write to <a href="#" data-email-user="support" data-email-domain="pifl-labs.com"><span class="email-text">support (at) pifl-labs.com</span></a>; we will respond within the time required by law. Your spending data is on your device only, so you can view, export and delete it yourself in the App. For information held by Google, we will help with your request, and you can also use Google's own tools (for example, resetting or deleting your advertising ID).</p>

                <h2>15. Security</h2>
                <p>Your spending data is kept in the App's private storage on your device and is protected by your device's own security settings, such as the screen lock. Because we do not run a server that stores your spending data, it cannot be leaked from our side.</p>

                <h2>16. Changes to this policy</h2>
                <p>We may update this policy when the App or the law changes. We will post the new version with a new effective date, and if the changes are significant we will let you know in the App or by other appropriate means.</p>

                <h2>17. Contact</h2>
                <p>PiFl Labs Co., Ltd. — 59 Jukseongseo-gil, Jeju, Republic of Korea — <a href="#" data-email-user="support" data-email-domain="pifl-labs.com"><span class="email-text">support (at) pifl-labs.com</span></a></p>
